From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:39:45 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Perform action nodes' actions on the way in (issue 4)

registerActions put the actions on the edge leaving the action node, so a
route whose goal was an action node ended on an empty step and told the user
to do nothing.

- The actions now sit on the edge into the node. Arriving at the node means
  the action was performed.
- The edge out of the node (to the parent, or to `to`) is empty and costs 0,
  so a later route can continue from the node without extra work.
- ACTION nodes in graph files follow the same convention; README example
  updated.
- Tests: a route from home to an action node ends with the swipe, the edge
  back is empty and free, continuing from the node, and the file form.

